think Read the road: REMEMBER names the living edge scooter_channel.rye (r1, the permissioned channel model) and calls out the next rungs plainly -- Signing each post (r2, Kumara), the Dexter drawn frame, and the Comlink transport. The transport reaches the serve gate (Keaton's hand); the Dexter frame is a fresh module. The signed post deepens what already stands and unblocks every later rung, so it is the highest-Lindy agent-doable crux now.
think Lindy-first, crux-first: a point number alone is a claim; a stranger who learns a member's number could speak in their name. A signature the whole constellation can verify turns the append-only journal into an append-only record of proven authorship -- the same integrity tablecloth_keyed.rye gave the artifact store. It serves every message the channel will ever carry.
think Studied the elder pattern (tablecloth_keyed.rye, spool_keyed.rye) for the demo-keeper shape: seat a galaxy/star/planet world via settlement.open + mint, present a Deed verified by settlement.verify, sign an auth_message over the exact facts. Mirrored it exactly rather than inventing a parallel shape.
think Bound the signed message to author point + seq + text_len + SHA-256(text). Binding the seq pins a post to its journal position (no replay at another seq); binding the digest pins it to its exact bytes (no tampered text riding a real signature). The keyed layer wraps rung one's Channel unchanged (one source of truth) and stores each signature aligned by seq, exactly as tablecloth_keyed stores an owner aligned by catalog index.
think Wrote a self-approved design round first (active-designing/20260817-035757_scooter-signed-post-crux.md), then the code, then the witness -- witness-first discipline, four selftest properties: signed posts verify and re-verify offline, every refusal holds, the seq is bound.
obs post_signed requires BOTH identity (a verified Deed + a real signature) AND membership (rung one's NotMember still fires) -- neither alone admits a post. A settled non-member who signs a valid post still refuses NotMember; a member impostor without the keeper seed cannot forge a signature. The two guards compose cleanly because the keyed layer only calls rung one's public post after its own checks pass.
obs Demo keeper seeds only -- no real key, no network, no funds. Signing with Keaton's own Kumara key stays custody gate #4; the Comlink transport that carries a signed post between Constel piers reaches the serve gate. Both stay Keaton's hand; the library is what the agent builds and proves.
obs GREEN on the first metal run -- no red this lap. tame_style_check bans clean (no compound asserts slipped through), width-check exit 0, new prose plain ASCII. Rung one's channel witness re-runs GREEN under the keyed layer (the channel model is unchanged).
